      "_comment": "Hand-placed themed regions (Greg's intent, 2026-05-16): vanilla mix in centre, massive mountain wall to the west, jungle pair (outer + deep separated by a swamp 'mollet') to the east, cursed_wastes far-north as the 'nether very far out'. Themes only apply OUTSIDE the radius floors — so a HARD-themed seed inside hard_min_radius behaves as vanilla MEDIUM until the player crosses the floor. Plain (no-theme) hard seeds at the other quadrants supply badlands/ice-spikes variety so themed seeds don't dominate the entire outer ring. Cell-boundary buffer (±200 blocks) automatically inserts a MEDIUM transition strip between any EASY↔HARD adjacency, so the themed-HARD cells never abut the easy core without a smooth Medium scallop in between.",
